  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1134 AM CST Thu Nov 26 2026\n\nHappy Thanksgiving everyone! Cooler temperatures to continue through the day, \nreaching the upper 50s to lower 60s this afternoon before cooling down once \nagain overnight to the low 40s. Winds will remain light and from the north \nthrough overnight before shifting from the south east as we head into the \nweekend. Cloud cover returns Friday and Saturday, temperatures are expected to \ngradually warm up to the mid 70s on Saturday before slightly cooling off Sunday \nfrom a cold front. Currently the cold front will move through mid morning \nSunday shifting winds from the north, temperatures are only expected to drop \nslightly. Lowering temperatures overnight to the low 50s across the region, \nbefore a warming trend continues through next week. \n\nRain chances stay low, inhibited by the lingering dry air and frequent fronts \nmoving through. PWAT values stay below climate normals for this time of year, \nalso keeping the rain chances to a minimum.",
